## Scripts (required)
| npm | purpose |
|-----|---------|
| `create:component` | scaffold base/industry/business (`vp-` class, types, style, stubs) |
| `generate:entry` | scan & rewrite component barrel `index.ts` — no manual mega-exports |
| `extract:i18n` | scan copy → regenerate `LocaleKey` schema + align **all** locale packs; missing key = bug/CI |
| `generate:locale-types` | emit `message-schema.ts` (`LocaleKey` / `LocaleMessages`) from zh-CN |
| `validate:catalog` | catalog ↔ base+industry coverage |
| `validate:styles` | every leaf has stable `dist/es/components/**/style.css` |
| `validate:maturity` | maturity JSON in sync (v3 signals; thinFormGaps empty) |
| `validate:v01` | v0.1 subset ↔ catalog ↔ maturity; Gallery badge subset-only |
| `score:maturity` | component depth score (v3) |
| `test:ssr` | SSR env + import + renderToString matrix |
| `generate:icons` | refresh icon catalog |
| `generate:vitepress-api` | regenerate docs component API stubs |
| `sync:example-zones` | sync example zone metadata |
| `build:skill` | build optional `amg-webui/skill` + `amg-webui/skill/core` entries |
| `build:theme` | build `amg-webui/theme` + `amg-webui/theme/core` + `theme/style.css` |
| `build:runtime` | runtime subpackages → `dist/{security,telemetry,lowcode,hooks,utils,…}/` |
| `build:ondemand` | multi-entry ESM → `dist/es/**` + leaf CSS side-entries |
| `build:styles` | leaf `style.css` only → `dist/es/components/{base\|industry}/<Name>/style.css` |
| `build:themes` | per-brand CSS → `dist/themes/<brand>.css` (`multi-theme` mode) |
| `build:dts` | types-only emit (`dts` mode) |
| `build:lib` | full: main + runtime + ondemand + styles + skill + theme + `generate:exports` |
| `generate:exports` | rewrite `package.json` `exports`/`files` to **dist-only** |
| `test:consumers` | `npm pack` + build `tests/consumer-{vite,webpack,nuxt}` |

Long-lived files under `scripts/`: `create-component` · `generate-entry` · `extract-i18n` · `generate-icon-catalog` · `generate-component-catalog` · `validate-component-catalog` · `score-component-maturity` · `sync-example-zones` · `generate-vitepress-api` · `classify-mvp` · `check-coverage` · `lucide-meta/`.  
**Do not** keep one-off `patch-*` / `upgrade-*` / `fix-*` / `inject-*` / demo-gen scripts in the repo after use — see `docs/ENGINEERING.md`.

Aliases:
- `@amg-webui/telemetry` → `packages/telemetry/index.ts` (file path, avoid dual Vite instances).
- `@amg-webui/skill` → `packages/skill/index.ts`; Core resolves to `packages/skill/core.ts`.
- `@amg-webui/theme/core` → `packages/theme/core.ts`; published `amg-webui/theme*` → `dist/theme/`.

Public Skill exports are `amg-webui/skill` and `amg-webui/skill/core`. The root `packages/index.ts` must not export Skill symbols; `build:skill` owns their independent JS and declaration output.

Public Theme exports are `amg-webui/theme`, `amg-webui/theme/core`, and `amg-webui/theme/style.css`. Theme Core must not touch `document` / `localStorage` directly — use Host / Storage adapters.

**Publish contract:** every public `exports` entry must resolve to compiled `dist/**` (JS + `.d.ts` + stable CSS). Never ship `packages/**/*.ts` / `.vue` as the consumer import target. On-demand chunks must import `amg-webui/*` (not `@amg-webui/*`). CI runs `test:consumers` after `build:lib`.

## Performance (non-negotiable defaults)
- **All list-like components** (DataTable, Tree, Select dropdown, infinite lists, virtualized menus): **virtual scroll ON by default** (opt-out only with explicit prop + docs warning).
- **Deep Tree-Shaking**: ESM side-effect free packages; per-component style entry; no fat re-export that pulls unused components; on-demand icons.
- Smaller bundles: runtime / component / style split; unplugin-vue-components (or equiv) resolver for consumers.
- Unmount cleans listeners/timers; shallow reactive for large row arrays.
- Telemetry **off by default**; when disabled, hot path early-return.
- Skill Runtime remains fully opt-in: the root build must contain no Skill registration, plugin install, or initialization side effect.

## Skill Runtime engineering boundary
- `packages/components/**` never imports `packages/skill`; Skills interact only through public host capabilities and scoped events.
- `packages/skill/core` is framework-neutral and has no direct dependency on components or `packages/telemetry`.
- A future Observer → Telemetry bridge must be supplied through a consumer adapter/interface; do not import Telemetry from Skill Core.
- Pipeline JSON v1 accepts declarative data and registered condition names only; never evaluate JSON text as JavaScript.
- SR1/SR2 remain experimental until verified. **SR3 built-ins and the example page are not implemented yet.**

## When adding a list component
Wire shared virtualizer hook first; never ship a full-DOM dump of unbounded data as default.

## When adding an interactive component
Call `trackEmit` beside business `emit`; default `telemetry: undefined` in `withDefaults` (Vue Boolean omit → `false` would skip all tracks).
